{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"Swidux","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"externalID":"Swidux","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Four optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, and analytics (Mixpanel or any backend)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The dispatch cycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identif